# Backend API base URL.
#
# Only needed if the built-in default (src/services/api.ts) doesn't fit your
# setup:
#   - iOS simulator / web: default (http://localhost:8000) works as-is.
#   - Android emulator: default (http://10.0.2.2:8000) works as-is.
#   - Physical device (Android or iOS) over Expo Go/Wi-Fi: 'localhost' and
#     '10.0.2.2' don't reach your dev machine — set this to your machine's
#     LAN IP instead (same Wi-Fi network as the device), and make sure the
#     backend is started with --host 0.0.0.0 (see README.md).
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.23:8000

# Google Maps API key — REQUIRED for the Map screen on both platforms
# (mobile native maps via android.config.googleMaps.apiKey, and the real
# Google Maps JavaScript API on web — see WebGoogleMap.tsx). Without it the
# map falls back to a visible "Could not load Google Maps" error state.
#
# Get one from Google Cloud Console (console.cloud.google.com):
#   1. Create/select a project, enable "Maps SDK for Android" and
#      "Maps JavaScript API".
#   2. Create an API key under APIs & Services > Credentials.
#   3. For a native build, the key only takes effect after `expo prebuild`
#      / a new EAS build — Expo Go substitutes its own key and ignores this
#      entirely, so changes here won't show up until you rebuild.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=your_key_here
